{"description":"`DedupeCheckByTitle`'s similarity path compares the incoming title against `NormalizeTitle(d.ID)` — the draft's slug — not against the title the draft was created from. The draft's stored `dedupeKey` is the hash of the normalized title, so the comparison is against a lossy proxy: a draft whose ID was truncated or disambiguated by the authoring layer is compared against a different string than the one it was captured with.","impact":"The similarity path is the only defence against duplicate drafts for titles that are not byte-identical, and it is comparing against a derived identifier rather than the recorded claim. Found while deciding the dedupe metric; not changed there because the metric and the input to the metric are separate decisions.","acceptanceCriteria":"- The similarity path compares against the title recorded in the draft's metadata, falling back to the slug only when no title was recorded.\n- A test covers a draft whose ID differs from its normalized title."}